(* 20_unit_checking.lep - how Lepthorn finds unit mistakes.

   The checker follows units before the program runs: from numbers
   with units, through variables, through * and /, and through
   function calls. These programs would be stopped before they start:

     ensure d = 2kg + 3m
       -> `+` needs the same unit on both sides, got kg and m

     show 1kg < 2m
       -> `<` needs the same unit on both sides, got kg and m

     suppose speed = 2m / 1s
     speed = 5kg
       -> 'speed' holds m/s, it cannot take a value in kg

     make add(a, b)
         done(a + b)
     done()
     show add(2kg, 3m)
       -> in this call to 'add': `+` needs the same unit on both sides,
          got kg and m

   When a unit is only known while the program runs (array items,
   shape fields, input), a mismatch stops the program with LEC8025.
   The program never goes on with a made-up value.

   Below is the correct version of each one. *)

ensure total_mass = 2kg + 3kg
show "total mass:" total_mass

show "lighter:" 1kg < 2kg

suppose speed = 2m / 1s
speed = 5m / 1s
show "new speed:" speed

make add(a, b)
    done(a + b)
done()
show "added:" add(2m, 3m)

(* a function result has a unit too: here a speed *)
make average_speed(distance, time)
    done(distance / time)
done()
ensure v = average_speed(100m, 20s)
show "average speed:" v
show "a bit faster:" v + 1mps
